Dear Editors,

Please consider our attached manuscript, "Regional medullary redox indices an=
d exploratory RT-qPCR findings in rats with atlantoaxial joint disorder", as =
a Short Communication in Physiological Research.

The study reports regional medullary SOD and MDA observations, together with =
auxiliary probe-associated fluorescence and exploratory Nox1/Nox4-targeted RT=
-qPCR estimates. The latter assays lack validation of tissue applicability or=
 target specificity; the manuscript does not present them as confirmed transc=
ript abundance or a NOX-dependent mechanism. Model and sham samples were coll=
ected at week 4, restoration samples at week 8, without a time-matched second=
-surgery control.

Each endpoint contains six records reported by the investigators to represent=
 different rats. Original animal-to-sample records are unavailable. Supplemen=
tary Table S2 documents two investigator-confirmed Plate annotation errors, t=
heir reported correction basis and the preserved Cq/reference pairing; the ex=
isting numerical analyses are unchanged.

Investigators report ethics approval AHUCM-rats-2022032, but the approval let=
ter and approved protocol cannot currently be supplied. Nine of 50 modeled ra=
ts died (18%). Postoperative analgesia was not administered, and no documente=
d justification or specific authorization for its omission was retained. Thes=
e unresolved welfare and documentation matters are explicitly disclosed.

Related published work and shared blood-pressure observations are identified =
in the manuscript and cover letter. All authors have approved the manuscript.=
 It has not been published previously and is not under consideration elsewher=
e. The authors declare no competing interests. Actual AI-assisted preparation=
 and analytical-code use are disclosed in the manuscript.

We provide the editable manuscript and complete PDF, two separate main figure=
s, cover letter, supplementary information containing detailed methods, exten=
ded results and editable Tables S1/S2, and available numerical inputs, source=
 exports and reproducible code. Please advise if supplementary items require =
an alternative format or placement.

Thank you for considering our submission.

Sincerely,
Zijian Wu and Youkui Lv
Corresponding authors, on behalf of all authors
wuzijian@ahtcm.edu.cn; lvyk126@126.com

